<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Las Cogotas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Las Cogotas is an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> hillfort near Cardeñosa in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avila">Ávila</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, and one of the main oppida of the Vettones. Excavated by Juan Cabré from 1927, it had two walled enclosures, a large cremation cemetery and stone boar sculptures. It gave its name to the Cogotas I and Cogotas II archaeological cultures of the Spanish Meseta.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/las-cogotas.jpg" alt="Las Cogotas" width="320" height="310" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sugaar at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iberia_Bronze.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
